@startuml 15-seq-identity
!include _style.iuml
title Identity and access: sign in, bind, grant, revoke

actor "Owner\n(key P)" as o
participant "Device\n(MUPPET)" as d
participant "Sign-in provider\n+ user's storage" as sso
participant "Host\n(session @review)" as t
actor "Collaborator\n(key Q)" as q

== identity: the key is the user ==
o -> d : sign in
d -> sso : SSO (Google, Apple, Mozilla)
sso --> d : private key for P,\nfrom the user's own storage
d -> t : hello (public key P)
t --> d : challenge (random nonce)
d -> t : prove: signature over the nonce
t -> t : P verified for this connection

== binding: the one signature that gives authorship ==
d -> t : bind (signed by P):\n"P owns client 7 on this document"
t -> t : record binding;\nops from client 7 on this\nconnection are P's
d -> t : update ops (7, …) — unsigned
note right of t : authorship comes from the binding,\nnot from per-op signatures

== authorisation: the creator grants by key ==
o -> d : share with Q
d -> t : grant (signed by P): Q may write @review
t -> t : record grant
q -> t : hello + prove (key Q), bind client 9
q -> t : update ops (9, …)
t -> t : Q holds write: admit

== revocation closes the door on arrival ==
d -> t : revoke (signed by P): Q
t -> t : from now, admit nothing new from Q
q -> t : update ops (9, …)\n(edited offline, claims earlier history)
t -> t : arrived after the revocation:\nnot admitted to @review
t --> q : ops kept on a fork owned by Q;\nnothing lost, nothing reaches @review
@enduml
